  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the first and $(2 n-1)$ th terms of an $\\mathrm{AP}$, GP and $\\mathrm{HP}$ are equal and their $n$ th terms are respectively $a, b, c,$ then always",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nBZit",
      "text": "$a=b=c$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wpwZD",
      "text": "$a \\geq b \\geq c$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Tyd8b",
      "text": "$a+c=b$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "89V1R",
      "text": "$a c-b^{2}=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because a, b$ and $c$ are respectively the $A M,$ GM and HM of first and $(2 n-1)$ th terms. and also, we know $A M \\geq G M \\geq H M$ and $A M \\cdot H M=G M^{2}$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad a \\geq b \\geq c$ and $a \\cdot c=b^{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
